---
const corpus = [
  { value: '222', label: 'complete demonstrations' },
  { value: '135,952', label: 'policy frames in the full corpus' },
  { value: '77', label: 'demonstrations in the strict subset' },
  { value: '68', label: 'physical evaluation rollouts' },
] as const;

const protocol = [
  { number: '01', title: 'Controlled task', body: 'A fixed-layout, low-contrast white cylinder is moved toward a white plate.' },
  { number: '02', title: 'Shared training basis', body: 'Both Diffusion Policy conditions use the same strict 77-demonstration subset, split into 65 training and 12 validation episodes.' },
  { number: '03', title: 'Narrow success rule', body: 'Object–plate contact defines success. Stable placement is not required, so this is not a full pick-and-place result.' },
] as const;
---

<section class="clothumi-evidence section-shell" aria-labelledby="clothumi-evidence-title">
  <div class="clothumi-evidence__heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Controlled evaluation · 68 physical rollouts</p>
    <div>
      <h3 id="clothumi-evidence-title">Hold the policy contract fixed. Change the tactile evidence.</h3>
      <p>
        The primary comparison isolates the added tactile pathway inside one Diffusion Policy family. Both
        conditions share wrist RGB, robot state, camera-relative actions, data subset, and rollout protocol;
        the tactile condition adds two causal histories encoded by frozen UniForce.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <dl class="tactile-corpus" aria-label="Tactile UMI dataset and evaluation scale">
    {corpus.map((item) => (
      <div>
        <dd>{item.value}</dd>
        <dt>{item.label}</dt>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <ol class="tactile-protocol" aria-label="Controlled experiment protocol">
    {protocol.map((item) => (
      <li>
        <span>{item.number}</span>
        <h4>{item.title}</h4>
        <p>{item.body}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <div class="clothumi-evidence__pipeline" aria-label="Tactile UMI policy comparison">
    <div class="evidence-path evidence-path--vision">
      <span>Shared condition</span>
      <strong>Wrist RGB + state</strong>
      <small>Frozen DINO ViT-B base with LoRA in the last four blocks · two observation steps</small>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence-path evidence-path--tactile">
      <span>Added condition</span>
      <strong>Dual tactile history</strong>
      <small>2 sides × 6 causal frames → frozen UniForce → 8 contact tokens</small>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence-path evidence-path--output">
      <span>Shared output</span>
      <strong>Diffusion Policy</strong>
      <small>Eight camera-relative 7D actions: translation, rotation, and gripper width</small>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="clothumi-results">
    <article>
      <p>Vision-only DP</p>
      <strong>10 <span>/ 34</span></strong>
      <div>
        <span>29.4% contact success</span>
        <small>Wilson 95% CI · 16.8–46.2%</small>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="clothumi-results__tactile">
      <p>UniForce + DP</p>
      <strong>14 <span>/ 34</span></strong>
      <div>
        <span>41.2% contact success</span>
        <small>Wilson 95% CI · 26.4–57.8%</small>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="clothumi-results__delta">
      <p>Observed difference</p>
      <strong>+4</strong>
      <div>
        <span>successful contacts</span>
        <small>+11.8 percentage points</small>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <div class="clothumi-evidence__qualification">
    <span>Evidence boundary</span>
    <p>
      The observed direction is encouraging but not statistically significant at this sample size (two-sided
      Fisher exact test, p = 0.447). This preliminary evaluation does not establish broad generalisation,
      cloth-manipulation performance, stable placement, or a causal mechanism for the improvement. The separate
      π0.5 integration is retained as systems evidence and is not folded into this 34-versus-34 comparison.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .tactile-corpus { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1px; margin-top: clamp(4rem, 7vw, 7rem); border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--line); }
  .tactile-corpus > div { min-height: 10rem; padding: clamp(1.25rem, 2.4vw, 2.35rem); background: var(--paper-deep); }
  .tactile-corpus dd { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 4.6vw, 5.3rem); letter-spacing: -.055em; line-height: .9; }
  .tactile-corpus dt { max-width: 13rem; margin-top: 1.4rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: .66rem; line-height: 1.5; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .07em; }
  .tactile-protocol { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--page-gutter); margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); list-style: none; }
  .tactile-protocol li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr; column-gap: 1rem; }
  .tactile-protocol li > span { grid-row: 1 / 3; color: var(--accent); font-size: .65rem; font-weight: 750; }
  .tactile-protocol h4 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 2rem); font-weight: 450; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .tactile-protocol p { margin-top: .75rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: .72rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .tactile-corpus { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .tactile-protocol { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .tactile-corpus { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .tactile-corpus > div { min-height: 8rem; }
  }
</style>
